WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
- We've got one more super
sweet story for the hour.

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.075
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.075 --> 00:00:07.371
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.371 --> 00:00:11.340
It takes utter commitment to
prepare and run a marathon.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.070
I wouldn't know, but I've heard it does.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.750
26 miles is a lot of miles to not drive.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.660
So after all that training,
it takes a truly big heart

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.370
to stop in the middle of the race

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.800
to rescue a kitten, which is so cute.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.510
That's just what one Chicago woman did

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.090
at the 20th mile marker, stopping her

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.340
from breaking her personal best time.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.710
And also, that's a lot of miles.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.220
Your body's gotta feel heavy
at that point to add a kitten.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.130
I don't care how much it
weighs, it seems like a lot.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.360
And before the race was over,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.160
she found that kitten a perfect new home.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.440
She did a lot, okay, during that race.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.300
We have that runner on the line right now,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.460
along with the mama of the rescued cat.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.620
Let's say hello to Sarah and Andrea

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.575
watching on NBC Chicago.

00:00:54.575 --> 00:00:55.695
(audience cheers)

00:00:55.695 --> 00:00:56.636
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:56.636 --> 00:00:58.505
- What's up y'all?

00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:01.540
- So Sarah, tell us
about finding the kitten.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.040
- Okay, I was at mile 20,
I'm focused on my race

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.250
and I remember running into this tunnel.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.870
I'm like, "Okay, I have six miles to go.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.780
I can get there," and I turn to the left.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.850
I see this little fluffy cat

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.160
in a pile of leaves looking terrified.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.890
I remember at that moment, it
was a split second decision,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.530
and I scooped this little baby up.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.870
Walking along the course,
I'm asking spectators,

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.280
can you take this cat?

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.180
I remember seeing Andrea in the crowd.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.150
She stepped forward and
she was so compassionate.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.640
She had said, "I'm a cat mom myself.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.750
I will re-home this cat.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.080
I'll love this cat with all my heart."

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.720
And at that point, I handed him off to her

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.068
and I haven't seen him since.

00:01:45.068 --> 00:01:48.750
- Ah, well Andre, that couldn't
have been your checklist

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.350
of things to do that day,
so how did that happen?

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.847
- So, not at all.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.340
I've been going out there
cheering on the runners

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.140
for 20 years with my family.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.310
So it was like a normal year,
and we were all out there

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.790
and this woman's in her running outfit.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.310
And she has this cute little
kitty and it's so adorable.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.327
And she's asking people in the crowd,

00:02:10.327 --> 00:02:11.880
"Can you give it a home?"

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.900
And then when we met, I was
like, in a split second,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.500
I thought to myself, "Can
I?" and I said, "Yes I can."

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.110
We brought him home and
we're very happy with him.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.170
His name's Casper and
he's doing very good.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.173
My family loves him, the kids love him.

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:34.200
And we're just so happy to
have him as part of our family.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.000
- Oh my gosh, I wish I weren't allergic.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.012
They're so cute.
(audience laughs)

00:02:38.012 --> 00:02:41.760
- Oh yeah, definitely cute.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.590
- Thank you so much, Sarah, for having

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.990
such a kind heart, also an athletic one.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.870
And Andrea, thank you
for taking the kitty in.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.070
Casper is super cute.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.890
Look at the little paw, oh my god.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.610
I'm liking your post right
now, but that's not all.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.440
Our season long partner, Pilot, pen makers

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.720
of Precise the go-to pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.910
want to celebrate animal
lovers just like y'all.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.207
So they're giving you $1,000,

00:03:04.207 --> 00:03:07.697
$500 each just for being rad.

00:03:07.697 --> 00:03:09.562
(audience applauds)

00:03:09.562 --> 00:03:11.348
Thank you guys so much.

00:03:11.348 --> 00:03:13.224
Thanks to all our guests this hour,

00:03:13.224 --> 00:03:16.915
Kevin James, Renata Notni,
Charles Esten, and Elana.

00:03:16.915 --> 00:03:19.615
And y'all have a great day
and if it's not, change it.

